values ('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001','How to Improve Your Writing with a Word Counter','improve-writing-with-word-counter','Learn how word count, sentence length, reading time, and keyword density can make your writing clearer and more useful.','How to Use a Word Counter to Improve Writing','Writing',array['word count','writing','productivity'],'Figimi Editorial',E'A word counter can do more than confirm an essay meets a limit. Used thoughtfully, its statistics reveal how a reader may experience your draft.\n\n## Start with the purpose\n\nDecide what the page must achieve before adding or cutting words. Word count is a constraint, not a quality score.\n\n## Watch sentence and paragraph rhythm\n\nMix concise statements with developed explanations and break dense mobile paragraphs into useful sections.\n\n## Use reading time as a promise\n\nIf a simple answer takes eight minutes to reach, move the answer earlier and organize supporting detail with headings.\n\n## Treat keyword density as a diagnostic\n\nUse repeated-term data to notice accidental repetition, not to stuff phrases for search engines.\n\n## Review aloud\n\nStatistics identify possible issues but cannot judge meaning. Read the final version, check claims, and ensure every paragraph helps the reader.','published','2026-01-15T09:00:00Z')
on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title,body=excluded.body,updated_at=now();
